5. ENVELOPE SEMANTICS

5.1 Definition

Definition 6 (Envelope). For each action a ∈ A, the envelope is a finite set of SPL predicates declared in ROM:

```
envelope(a) = ⟨ precond_1, …, precond_k,
                magnitude_bounds,
                rate_bounds,
                duration_bounds,
                abort_condition ⟩
```

Each element is an SPL predicate. The envelope holds if all elements hold.

5.2 Envelope Components

Component Meaning Example
Preconditions State requirements s.world.brake_pressure > 0
Magnitude bounds Action parameter limits abs(a.delta) <= max_delta
Rate bounds Change rate limits abs(a.delta - s.prev.delta) <= rate_max
Duration bounds Time limits a.duration <= duration_max
Abort condition When to abort mid-action s.world.emergency_stop = TRUE

5.3 The Envelope Invariant

Proposition A5-E (Envelope Invariant). If VERIFY returns PASS, the committed action a satisfies s ∈ envelope(a).

Proof. By step 4 of the VERIFY algorithm, envelope evaluation is explicit. If any envelope predicate fails, VERIFY returns FAIL. If VERIFY returns PASS, all envelope predicates held. □

---

6. INVARIANT CHECKING

6.1 Definition

Definition 7 (Invariant Set). I ⊆ S is declared per deployment (A4 §6). Each invariant is an SPL predicate over state.

6.2 Prospective Evaluation

Rule: VERIFY evaluates invariants over the post-state s' = δ(s, a), not the current state.

This is what makes VERIFY a safety gate. It verifies the consequence of the action before committing it.

6.3 The Invariant Preservation Theorem

Theorem A5-I (Invariant Preservation). If every state entering VERIFY is in I, and VERIFY returns PASS for the proposed action, then the state after COMMIT is in I.

Proof. By step 6 of VERIFY, all invariants are evaluated over the post-state s'. If any fails, VERIFY returns FAIL, and the action is refused. If VERIFY returns PASS, all invariants hold over s'. Therefore the post-state is in I. □

This is the load-bearing safety theorem. It is what makes the invariant set preserved by construction, not by hope.

