7. COST MODEL

7.1 Per-Predicate Cost

Rule: Each SPL predicate has a declared cycle cost. The cost is bounded by c_max (Corollary A5-D1).

For typical deployments: c_max ≤ 256 cycles.

7.2 VERIFY Total Cost

VERIFY evaluates:

· 1 precondition set (k_p predicates).
· 1 envelope set (k_e predicates).
· |I| invariants.

Total cost:

```
c_verify = (k_p + k_e + |I|) × c_max
```

For typical values (k_p = k_e = 4, |I| = 8, c_max = 64): c_verify = 16 × 64 = 1024 cycles.

Note: This exceeds the A1 declared VERIFY cost of 40 cycles. This is an open tension (see §9).

7.3 Optimization Strategies

To reduce c_verify:

1. Predicate sharing — deduplicate predicates across preconditions, envelope, invariants.
2. Compile-time folding — constant atoms folded at burn time.
3. Short-circuit ordering — most-likely-to-fail predicates first.
4. Memoization — cache invariant evaluations for identical post-states.

These reduce c_verify in practice. The bound remains c_max.

