8. VERDICT AND REFUSAL SEMANTICS

8.1 Verdicts

Verdict Meaning FSM Transition
PASS All checks passed COMMIT
FAIL(0x-PRECONDITION-UNMET) Preconditions did not hold REFUSE_ACT
FAIL(0x-ENVELOPE-VIOLATED) Envelope bounds exceeded REFUSE_ACT
FAIL(0x-INVARIANT-VIOLATED) Post-state would leave I REFUSE_ACT

8.2 Determinism of Verdicts

Proposition A5-V (Verdict Determinism). For the same (s, a), VERIFY returns the same verdict.

Proof. By Theorem A5-Det (SPL determinism), every predicate evaluation is deterministic. VERIFY is a composition of predicate evaluations and short-circuit logic. Composition of deterministic functions is deterministic. □

8.3 Totality of Verdicts

Proposition A5-VT (Verdict Totality). For every (s, a) ∈ S × A, VERIFY returns exactly one verdict.

Proof. By Theorem A5-T (SPL totality), every predicate is defined for every state. Therefore every step of VERIFY is defined. Every step returns a verdict. The algorithm terminates because the predicate set is finite (SPL compilation §2.7). □

