9. OPEN DESIGN TENSIONS

Honest labeling. These are unresolved in A5 v1.0.

# Question Impact
1 VERIFY cost vs. A1 declared cost. A1 declares VERIFY at 40 cycles; A5's cost model requires ~1024. Either A1 must increase the VERIFY budget, or A5 must tighten c_max, or optimizations are mandatory. Affects sub-task WCET (A1 §5.1).
2 Predicate language expressiveness. SPL cannot express comparisons across time (e.g., "brake pressure was below X in the last 5 seconds"). Is that acceptable, or is a temporal extension needed? If needed, temporal predicates require bounded history (A7).
3 Range variable semantics. forall i in [0..N]: P(s.mem[i]) — does s.mem[i] access the SRAM window? If so, the window size bounds N. Interacts with A7.
4 Quantifier over identifier sets. forall t in {MATH, LAW, MED}: P(t) — how is the set membership declared? Needs a formal declaration mechanism.
5 Envelope composition. If an action is a composed plan step (A3), the envelope must account for the whole sub-plan. Is the envelope declared per plan or per step? Interacts with A3 §5.
6 Compile-time verification. Who verifies that all SPL predicates compile correctly? A burn-time verifier is needed. Future spec (A2 or a new sub-spec).
7 The c_atom value. What is the actual cost of a single atom evaluation on the target hardware? Deployment-specific.
8 Cross-tile predicate scope. Can a predicate in tile A reference state owned by tile B? Interacts with isolation (A4 §5, A6).

None are fatal. All must be resolved before A5 v2.0.

