10. FORMAL PROPERTIES

The five properties A5 contributes to the Verifiable Agency Theorem:

Property A5.1 (Decidability). Every SPL predicate is decidable in bounded time (Theorem A5-D).

Property A5.2 (Determinism). Every SPL predicate is deterministic (Theorem A5-Det).

Property A5.3 (Totality). Every SPL predicate is total (Theorem A5-T).

Property A5.4 (Invariant Preservation). VERIFY preserves the invariant set I (Theorem A5-I).

Property A5.5 (Verdict Determinism & Totality). VERIFY returns exactly one deterministic verdict for every (s, a) (Propositions A5-V, A5-VT).

These are the A5 obligations to the Verifiable Agency Theorem. Each closes a specific assumption in the proof.

