11. TLA+ SKELETON

```tla
--------------------------- MODULE STT1024_A5_Verify ---------------------------
EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, Sequences

CONSTANTS
    S,           \* State space (A4)
    A,           \* Action library (A2)
    I,           \* Invariant set ⊆ S
    D_pred,      \* Max predicate depth
    r_max,       \* Max quantifier range
    c_atom,      \* Atom evaluation cost
    delta        \* State transition (A4)

\* The SPL grammar as a tagged union.
SPL == [
    kind : {"atom", "not", "and", "or", "forall", "exists"},
    left : SPL,           \* for binary connectives
    right : SPL,          \* for binary connectives
    sub : SPL,            \* for unary connectives and quantifiers
    var : STRING,         \* for quantifiers
    range : {a, b \in Int : a <= b},   \* for quantifiers
    atom : [field : STRING, op : STRING, val : Int]
]

\* Evaluation semantics — deterministic, total.
eval(p, s) ==
    CASE p.kind = "atom"    -> EvalAtom(p.atom, s)
      [] p.kind = "not"     -> ~eval(p.sub, s)
      [] p.kind = "and"     -> eval(p.left, s) /\ eval(p.right, s)
      [] p.kind = "or"      -> eval(p.left, s) \/ eval(p.right, s)
      [] p.kind = "forall"  -> \A i \in p.range.a..p.range.b : eval(Subst(p.sub, p.var, i), s)
      [] p.kind = "exists"  -> \E i \in p.range.a..p.range.b : eval(Subst(p.sub, p.var, i), s)

\* Decidability: cost is bounded.
cost(p) ==
    CASE p.kind = "atom"    -> c_atom
      [] p.kind = "not"     -> cost(p.sub) + 1
      [] p.kind = "and"     -> cost(p.left) + cost(p.right) + 1
      [] p.kind = "or"      -> cost(p.left) + cost(p.right) + 1
      [] p.kind = "forall"  -> (p.range.b - p.range.a + 1) * cost(p.sub) + (p.range.b - p.range.a + 1)
      [] p.kind = "exists"  -> (p.range.b - p.range.a + 1) * cost(p.sub) + (p.range.b - p.range.a + 1)

c_max == D_pred * r_max * c_atom

THEOREM Decidability == \A p \in SPL : cost(p) <= c_max

\* VERIFY algorithm
VERIFY(s, a) ==
    LET p_pre  == a.preconditions
        p_env  == a.envelope
        s_next == delta[s, a]
    IN IF ~eval(p_pre, s)         THEN "FAIL_PRE"
       ELSE IF ~eval(p_env, s)     THEN "FAIL_ENV"
       ELSE IF ~(\A i \in I : eval(i, s_next)) THEN "FAIL_INV"
       ELSE "PASS"

\* Invariant preservation theorem
THEOREM InvariantPreservation ==
    \A s \in I, a \in A :
        VERIFY(s, a) = "PASS" => delta[s, a] \in I

=============================================================================
```

The theorems Decidability and InvariantPreservation are the A5 obligations. Both are paper-proven above; both require model-checking for specific instances and proof-assistant discharge for the general case.

